# The build context is the whole repo (the Dockerfile selects one project via a
# build arg), so excluding these is not an optimisation — a Windows-built .venv
# copied into a Linux image would shadow the installed packages and break the
# container in a confusing way.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Local state, never belongs in an image
**/.env
**/.chroma/
**/traces/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite3

.git/
.github/
docs/
*.md
!*/*/README.md
